WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:01.530
(audience clapping)
- We always like to close out

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.610
with something super cool

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.020
we found on social media,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.880
and just like everywhere else,

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.910
there is no shortage of
love for Dolly online.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.515
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:10.515 --> 00:00:11.536
(dynamic music)

00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:12.810
(audience cheers)

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.750
I always appreciate how inventive teachers

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.280
can get with their classes.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.230
There's one national elementary teacher

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.690
who uses Dolly Parton's life and songs

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.730
to teach all sorts of important lessons

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.290
to shape kids' lives.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.760
No wonder she's been named

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.140
a Music Teacher of Excellence

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.240
by the Country Music Association

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.410
three times.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.600
We have this educator
on the line right now

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.360
watching on NewsChannel
5 Nashville at three.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.346
Hi, Alice.

00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:39.179
(audience cheers)

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:40.230
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.790
- What's up? So how did you,

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.620
first of all thank you
for being an educator.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.450
You are an angel for doing that

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.490
but how did you come up with this?

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.590
- Well, I'm originally from New Jersey

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.960
and I grew up with samba

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.430
and classical music in my house,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.230
so country folk was not something

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.940
I really was familiar with,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.000
and when I moved in 2015 to Nashville,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.770
I started seeing lots of

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.480
Dolly Parton everywhere and I heard

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.780
about her and her generous donation

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.540
with the Gatlinburg fire,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.250
and I just thought, "Wow, what a person,"

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.170
and the more I got to know her

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.370
and learned about her story,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.160
I realized she was a great
role model for our students.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.350
A lot of what Dolly
talks about in her songs

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.750
is what the students
are thinking and feeling

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.210
and it just really creates a place

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.580
for them when they sing her
songs and listen to them.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.810
- I mean, it's so wonderful.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.730
I get it, even as a kid I related that way

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.960
'cause I don't come from, you know,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.920
I come from humble beginnings,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.320
so it was like, but she kind of made kids

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.480
think and feel like we
could accomplish anything.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.130
We could make it because she did.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:41.340
And so how are the kids
impacted by your Dolly lessons?

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.113
- A lot of them can really connect.

00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:46.170
Turns out a lot of their
family members love Dolly too,

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.050
so the next week they'll say
like, "You know, I went home.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.060
I shared about my lesson and we had

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.680
family singing of Dolly Parton.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.150
We had a dance party.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.320
We got to read the books."

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.330
And she just really brings the literacy

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.340
into the homes to encouraging the reading

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.440
with the parents and the children

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.640
and just their relatives,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.800
but students really

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.140
see a little bit of themselves in Dolly,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.880
and they take it with them

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.620
when they do their own songwriting,

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.660
and they can really feel
like they have a place

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.540
where they can express their
emotions and their dreams,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.920
just like how Dolly did.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.330
- Oh, I love that.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.213
Thank you so much Alice.

00:02:20.213 --> 00:02:21.046
(audience applauds)
This is such a cool way

00:02:21.046 --> 00:02:22.200
to teach kids.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.336
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:24.336 --> 00:02:25.464
(emoji dings)

00:02:25.464 --> 00:02:26.490
And that's not all, ma'am.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.890
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.140
the go to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.150
want to celebrate those creating

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.370
and teaching fearlessly just like you,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.810
so they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.141
How's that sound?

00:02:38.141 --> 00:02:40.253
(audience claps and cheers)

00:02:40.253 --> 00:02:43.312
- Okay. (laughs)

00:02:43.312 --> 00:02:44.145
I love it.

00:02:44.145 --> 00:02:44.978
- Thank you so much, Allison.
(audience cheers louder)

00:02:44.978 --> 00:02:45.811
Thank you.

00:02:45.811 --> 00:02:47.490
A huge thank you to Dolly Parton

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.320
for spending the whole hour with us.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.670
I love her so much.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.990
Love her even more now.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.950
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.950
and if it's not, well try and change it.

